{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "When you say \"total overtime hours per month for the entire workforce cannot exceed 20 hours per worker,\" do you mean the overtime cap is 20 hours per individual worker per month (so total workforce overtime can be up to 20 × number of workers), or that the sum of overtime hours across all workers combined is capped at 20 hours per month?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single clarification regarding the interpretation of the overtime cap constraint, presenting two mutually exclusive options for the same policy definition."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 2,
  "is_atomic": false,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "For the workforce, can you hire and fire workers in any month (including January)?",
    "Is the workforce level for a month determined by the number of workers on staff during that month (i.e., hires and firings happen at the start of the month and affect that month's production capacity)?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response contains two semantically independent questions: one asking about the timing/frequency of hiring and firing (whether it can happen in any month), and another asking about the timing of when those changes take effect relative to production capacity (start of month vs. during the month). A user could answer the first without answering the second."
}

